  "markscheme": {
    "html": "<section class=\"markscheme-part\" data-label=\"a\"><p><strong>a</strong></p><p>- Identify that energy stored is the area under the force-compression graph: <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"E_p = \\frac{1}{2} Fx\"></span> [1 mark]<br/>- Substitute values from the graph: <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"E_p = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 54 \\times 0.12 = 3.24 \\text{ J}\"></span> [1 mark]</p></section><section class=\"markscheme-part\" data-label=\"b\"><p><strong>b</strong></p><p>- Calculate the kinetic energy of the ball: <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"E_k = \\frac{1}{2}mv^2 = 0.5 \\times 0.040 \\times 11^2 = 2.42 \\text{ J}\"></span> [1 mark]<br/>- Calculate the efficiency: <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\eta = \\frac{E_{\\text{out}}}{E_{\\text{in}}} = \\frac{2.42}{3.24} \\approx 0.747\"></span> or <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"74.7\\%\"></span> [1 mark]</p></section>"
  },
  "paper": "paper_2",
  "question": {
    "html": "<p>The graph below shows the variation of the force <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"F\"></span> applied to a spring in a ball launcher with its compression <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"x\"></span>. A ball of mass <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"40 \\text{ g}\"></span> is placed in the launcher.</p><p><figure data-asset-id=\"fig_01\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 1\" src=\"asset:fig_01\"/></figure></p><section class=\"question-part\" data-label=\"a\"><p><strong>a</strong> </p>Using the graph, determine the elastic potential energy stored in the spring when it is compressed by <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"0.12 \\text{ m}\"></span>.<p>[2]</p></section><section class=\"question-part\" data-label=\"b\"><p><strong>b</strong> </p>The launcher is fired. On leaving the launcher, the ball has a speed of <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"11 \\text{ m\\,s}^{-1}\"></span>. Calculate the efficiency of the launcher in transferring energy to the ball.<p>[2]</p></section>"
  },
